// crates/nikaia-std/src/runtime/text_normal.nika
//
// **Unicode's normalisation forms** (ADR-320 D8), written in Nikaia: the
// enum `s.normalized(form)` takes.
//
// `src/text_normal.rs` re-exports `Form` as `nikaia_std::text::Form` and
// keeps `normalized`, whose tables are the `unicode-normalization` crate's
// and follow Unicode's versions. `std.contracts` writes the type's entry by
// hand.

/// One of Unicode's four normalisation forms (UAX #15).
///
/// `Nfc` composes and `Nfd` decomposes, by canonical equivalence; `Nfkc` and
/// `Nfkd` do the same by compatibility as well, so `ﬁ` becomes `fi`.
pub enum Form {
    /// Canonical decomposition, then canonical composition.
    Nfc,
    /// Canonical decomposition.
    Nfd,
    /// Compatibility decomposition, then canonical composition.
    Nfkc,
    /// Compatibility decomposition.
    Nfkd,
}
